== Peronal Data Protection Law ==


== Article No. 27: Data Collection Research & Statistics ==

Article 27 of the Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) of Saudi Arabia is about using personal data for scientific, research, or statistical purposes. It allows such processing without the consent of the data subject under certain conditions.



Key Points


Q.1 In which scenarios can personal data be processed for scientific, research, or statistical purposes without the consent of the data subject?

If the data does not identify the data subject specifically (Article 27).

If the data subject’s identity is removed before processing or disclosure, provided the data is not sensitive (Article 27).

If processing is required by another law or by an agreement previously accepted by the data subject (Article 27).

Q.2 What limitation applies to processing sensitive data under Article 27?


Sensitive data cannot be processed for scientific, research, or statistical purposes without explicit consent (Article 27).


Q.3 Which regulation provides detailed rules for processing data for scientific, research, or statistical purposes?

Article 30 of the Implementing Regulation provides detailed guidelines for such processing (Article 30 of Implementing Regulation).

Q.4 What are the basic requirements for processing personal data for research or statistical purposes?

Clearly record the purpose of processing (Article 30 of Implementing Regulation).

Collect only the minimum level of data required (Article 30 of Implementing Regulation).

Pseudonymize the data if it does not affect the research or statistical purpose (Article 30 of Implementing Regulation).

Ensure that processing does not harm the rights or interests of the data subject (Article 30 of Implementing Regulation).
